# One-time migration runners carry a hardcoded shared-secret token and are
# deleted from the server the moment they've run. The schema they apply is
# documented in api/migrations.sql, so keeping them out of a public repo
# costs nothing. (api/_migrate_seo.php predates this rule and is already
# tracked; removing it now would not scrub it from history anyway.)
api/_migrate_crm.php
api/_migrate_crm2.php
api/_migrate_crm_emoji_fix.php
api/_migrate_sections.php

# Local-only: server backups (contain real secrets) and hosting credentials.
# Never commit these — config.secrets.php.live + handover_report.md hold live
# JWT/DB/FTP secrets.
_deploy/
hosting details (ignore in github)/

# Runtime-only: enquiry spool (unsent leads) and PHP error log. Never committed.
api/spool/
api/logs/
